From: lmoresi <louis.moresi@anu.edu.au>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 16:01:19 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 1/9] The JIT builds under TMPDIR and removes its build
 directory once loaded

compile_and_load built every extension in a directory under a hard-coded
/tmp and nothing removed it: one fn_ptr_ext_<hash>_<pid>_<time>_<n> per
compile per rank, a dozen or more inodes each. They filled a Linux server's
/tmp (a tmpfs of 1,048,576 inodes) and stopped every session on it.

The directory is now made by tempfile.mkdtemp, so TMPDIR is honoured, and
getext removes it after the module is loaded and stored in the disk cache.
The loaded module does not need it: the mapped .so survives its unlink, on
macOS as on Linux (test_0903 solves with kernels whose build directory is
gone). debug=True keeps it for reading the sources; a failed build keeps it
because the error names it. The removal is rank-local and best-effort and
decides nothing, so the ranks cannot diverge on it.

test_0903 (tier B) fails before the change: the build directories were
under /tmp, not TMPDIR, and remained.

Underworld development team with AI support from Claude Code
